.TH GENFI 1 "May 2026" "genfi 0.1.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
genfi \- generate folder icons from contained video frames and photos

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genfi
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genfi
recursively scans directories for folders containing video files and/or photos,
extracts frames from videos (or uses photos directly), composes them into a
folder-shaped icon, and sets it as the folder's custom Nautilus icon using \fBgio\fR(1).

Videos are always used first. Remaining frame slots are filled by photos.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \fIPATH\fR
Root directory to scan. Defaults to the current directory (\fB.\fR).

.TP
.B \-\-version
Show program version and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-clean
Remove custom icons from all processed folders under \fIPATH\fR and delete generated image files.

.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Full uninstall: revert all folder icons, remove cache, config, and generated files.

.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without making any changes.

.TP
.B \-\-force
Regenerate icons even if the folder content hasn't changed.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-restart
Skip the Nautilus refresh step at the end.

.TP
.B \-\-max\-frames \fIN\fR
Maximum number of media frames to include per folder icon. Default: 4.

.TP
.B \-\-size \fIN\fR
Output icon resolution in pixels (square). Default: 512.

.TP
.B \-\-frame\-position \fIF\fR
Position in video to grab frame, as a fraction (0.0 to 1.0). Default: 0.1 (10% into the video).

.TP
.B \-\-crop \fIMODE\fR
How to handle non-square frames. Modes: \fBfill\fR (stretch), \fBfit\fR (letterbox), \fBcenter\fR (center-crop). Default: center.

.TP
.B \-\-types \fITYPE\fR
Media types to include: \fBboth\fR (videos first, then photos), \fBvideo\fR (videos only), \fBphoto\fR (photos only). Default: both.

.TP
.B \-\-workers \fIN\fR
Number of parallel ffmpeg workers for video frame extraction. Default: 4.

.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show detailed output including debug information.

.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress all output except errors.

.SH CONFIGURATION
A configuration file at \fB~/.config/genfi/genfi.toml\fR can set persistent defaults. Example:

.nf
max_frames = 4
icon_size = 256
frame_position = 0.15
crop_mode = "center"
media_types = "both"
workers = 2
.fi

CLI flags always override configuration file values.

.SH CACHE
Results are cached in \fB~/.cache/thumbnails/genfi/genfi_cache.db\fR.
Folders that haven't changed (based on mtime and media file hash) are skipped
unless \fB\-\-force\fR is used.

.SH NAUTILUS REFRESH
After generating icons, \fBgenfi\fR automatically refreshes Nautilus:

1. Touches each processed folder (best-effort metadata re-read)
2. If \fBxdotool\fR is available, sends F5 to open Nautilus windows
3. Otherwise runs \fBnautilus -q\fR (graceful quit; Nautilus auto-restarts on next open)

Use \fB\-\-no\-restart\fR to skip this step.

.SH NAUTILUS INTEGRATION
Install the Nautilus script for right-click integration:

.nf
cp nautilus-scripts/genfi ~/.local/share/nautilus/scripts/
chmod +x ~/.local/share/nautilus/scripts/genfi
.fi

Then right-click any folder in Nautilus, select "Scripts", then "genfi".

.SH UNINSTALL

.nf
# Remove pip package
pip uninstall genfi

# Or use the bundled script
./uninstall.sh          # Remove genfi files
./uninstall.sh \-\-all     # Also revert all folder icons
.fi

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.I Python >= 3.11
.TP
.I ffmpeg
Required for video frame extraction.
.TP
.I Pillow
Installed automatically via pip.
.TP
.I xdotool (optional)
If installed, used for non-disruptive Nautilus refresh via F5 key.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Generate icons (videos + photos):
.B genfi

.TP
Photos only:
.B genfi \-\-types photo ~/Pictures

.TP
Generate icons with verbose output:
.B genfi \-v ~/Videos

.TP
Preview changes without applying:
.B genfi \-\-dry\-run ~/Videos

.TP
Use 2 frames, 256px icons:
.B genfi \-\-max\-frames 2 \-\-size 256 ~/Videos

.TP
Skip Nautilus refresh:
.B genfi \-\-no\-restart ~/Videos

.TP
Remove all generated icons:
.B genfi \-\-clean ~/Videos

.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/genfi/genfi.toml
User configuration file.

.TP
.B ~/.cache/thumbnails/genfi/genfi_cache.db
Cache database.

.TP
.B ~/.folder-icon.png
Generated icon file stored inside each processed folder.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gio (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR nautilus (1)

